  gc_row(id: GcN12c, what: "amd-smi power-cap, clock and temperature queries and effects.",
    home: GcCreates { module: "extdeps.amd.amd_smi" },
    done: "each operation parses a captured output and refuses an unsupported one, in a witness.", needs: []),
  gc_row(id: GcN12d, what: "The R9700 catalog row, with every figure cited.",
    home: GcCreates { module: "extdeps.gpu.amd" },
    done: "the card resolves to a cited catalog row.", needs: []),
  gc_row(id: GcN12e, what: "Install the R9700 pair and run the same leg on its host, with its receipts and selection.",
    home: GcCreates { module: "gunbc.host.gpu_card_converge" },
    done: "both cards' readbacks hold, and the leg gained rows only.", needs: [GcD3, GcN7, GcN8, GcN10, GcN12a, GcN12b, GcN12c, GcN12d]),
  gc_row(id: GcGoal, what: "Every in-bound card converges.", home: GcExtends { symbol: "gunbc.plans.gpu_card_host_program::gpu_card_in_bound" },
    done: "no census row is committed, and every in-bound row's readback holds on its host.", needs: [GcN11, GcN12e]),
]

fn gpu_card_host_program_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Draft under operator design, originally reviewed as #15207; converge leg unstarted. Model before implementation. Typed census/graph rows below remain the standing source; [original design and measured receipts](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/gpu_card_host_program.dag) retains the full earlier inventory. One lane under the Mt. Collins worker; no work outside this graph."),
    h2(text: "0. Bound and working census"),
    p(text: "`gunbc.plans.gpu_card_host_program::gpu_card_in_bound` includes every card installed in or committed to an operator-owned fleet host, whether serving or not. Finish only when no row remains merely committed and every in-bound card independently reads back converged through the real path. gpu_card_working_census is an operator-confirmation reading (D0), not final authority: N0a moves census and predicate to gunbc.fleet, then imports them here. Passive A16s need fan zones; actively cooled cards need accelerator guards. No unconsumed model or measurement enters this bound."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "count"), cell(text: "product"), cell(text: "slots"), cell(text: "host"), cell(text: "membership")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: map(gpu_card_working_census, r => gc_census_projection(r: r)),
    },
    h2(text: "1. Goal"),
    p(text: "One vendor-neutral converge leg gets driver/pinned release, power cap/persistence/idle state, physical card/fan placement and cooling reach right, then independently reads them back or refuses located. NVIDIA A16/Ada/Blackwell and committed AMD R9700 cards use the same leg; adding AMD must need rows, not another architecture."),
    h2(text: "2. Existing homes and ownership"),
    p(text: "Extend extdeps.gpu catalog/board admission and cited NVIDIA/AMD driver/tool upstreams; gunbc.fleet physical inventory, fan wiring/tach expectation and host identity; product.fleet_fan_policy; fleet_fan_converge_routes; gunbc.serving.home_serving_power_policy; and std.decision selection as already consumed by product.mt_collins_power_policy. #12500 browser-toolchain and #15177 GPU-container-toolchain give the observe/converge/readback pattern; toolkit currently assumes a driver and must consume this leg’s loaded-driver readback."),
    h2(text: "3. Measurements and their standing"),
    p(text: "These are observations of one host/configuration, not upstream facts. Device minimum becomes an upstream fact only with a vendor citation. Preserve the exact receipts below. Other in-bound cards lack these measurements; section 6 produces them by installed position. File/update recurring-failure rows for lid-off Xid and for adjacent-board overheating in this slot pitch and chassis airflow (evidence for that configuration, not a rule against adjacency); nonuniform temperatures require GPU position within a board, not only slot identity."),
    TableBlock {
      header: t3(a: "reading (A16, one GPU unless stated)", b: "figure", c: "standing"),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        t3(a: "no process", b: "P8, 13.6–15.6 W, 210 / 405 MHz", c: "measured, range across GPUs"),
        t3(a: "bare CUDA context, no work", b: "P0, 27.0 W, 1755 / 6251 MHz", c: "measured. This happens with any context, not only Strata's"),
        t3(a: "Strata loaded, idle", b: "P0, 27.0 W", c: "measured"),
        t3(a: "Strata loaded, memory clock locked to its minimum", b: "P8, about 12.5–15.6 W, warm state retained, wake about 1–2 s", c: "measured. The wake time is approximate"),
        t3(a: "minimum power limit", b: "48.75 W, maximum 62.50 W. `-pl 40` exits 2 with \"not a valid power limit which should be between 48.75 W and 62.50 W\" and leaves the cap unchanged", c: "measured on driver 595.91.07; not cited to NVIDIA"),
        t3(a: "supported clocks, GPU 0", b: "memory 405 or 6251 MHz; at 405 MHz memory, graphics 405–420 MHz. `-lmc 405,405` accepted at runtime; `-lmi` is not a recognized option (exit 255)", c: "measured on driver 595.91.07"),
        t3(a: "48.75 W against the stock 62.5 W, in this chassis", b: "same throughput: the cards hit their thermal limit before the cap", c: "measured on one cooling configuration"),
        t3(a: "core clock locked to 900 MHz", b: "about 20% lower throughput", c: "measured"),
        t3(a: "warm decode bottleneck, 16 GB engine", b: "about 60% memory bandwidth, about 38% SM; PCIe about 0.5 GB/s average with 7 GB/s bursts", c: "measured, one sensitivity run"),
        t3(a: "lid off", b: "87–92 °C at idle, then Xid 154 on six GPUs", c: "incident"),
        t3(a: "two boards in adjacent slots of the H11 (its slot pitch and chassis airflow)", b: "96–99 °C under load at minimum clocks; one GPU dropped off the bus", c: "incident"),
        t3(a: "SLOT2 + SLOT6, Ada removed, 3 × 120 mm on FANB, idle and partial load", b: "48–81 °C", c: "measured"),
        t3(a: "same placement, full load, FANB at 100%", b: "the first GPU of each board (bus 85/86 and c5/c6) reaches 87–88 °C with SW thermal slowdown (210–585 MHz); the other GPUs stay at 56–78 °C", c: "measured. Heat is not uniform within a board: it depends on the GPU's position"),
        t3(a: "installed driver on the H11", b: "`nvidia-driver-595-server-open` 595.91.07-0ubuntu0.24.04.1 (server branch, open kernel modules), on Ubuntu 24.04", c: "read from dpkg"),
        t3(a: "BMC and fan state on the H11", b: "Supermicro BMC firmware 1.52 on an H11SSL-i/c/nc; fan mode reads 0x01 (Full); zone 0 duty 0x1d (29%), zone 1 duty 0x64 (100%); the specimen loop writes zone duty with `raw 0x30 0x70 0x66 0x01 <zone> <duty>`", c: "read in-band through ipmitool"),
        t3(a: "RTX 2000 Ada, idle with the engine loaded", b: "4.1–4.2 W per card on one reading; about 4–8 W across readings. It downclocks without help", c: "measured"),
      ]
    },
    h2(text: "4. Host-written specimens to replace"),
    p(text: "Delete these in the real cutover and reproduce their required behavior as controls: /usr/local/sbin/a16-fan.sh + a16-fan.service (BMC Full, zone 0 CPU/zone 1 hottest GPU, /etc/a16-fan.zone0 override); a16-idle-memclock.sh/service; h11-strata@<bus>.service’s PCI 0x25b6 / 48.75 W startup cap, which belongs to power policy rather than the engine; and hand-set nvidia-smi -pm 1. Ubuntu nvidia-compute-utils-595-server’s static daemon unit starts --no-persistence-mode, so running nvidia-persistenced does not prove persistence and reboot loses the hand setting. Engine units, strata-pool on srv3 and router configuration belong to serving deployment."),
    h2(text: "5. Model and converge contract"),
    p(text: "Upstream owners: extend extdeps.nvidia.system_management_interface power draw/limit/min/max, P-state, clocks, persistence, supported clocks/event reasons and power/persistence/clock lock-reset operations. Unsupported capability and unrecognized release-specific option are distinct arms (-lmi refused on 595.91.07 despite generic documentation). extdeps.nvidia.persistence_daemon owns flag semantics; extdeps.systemd.systemctl reads ExecStart and extdeps.systemd.service_exec.exec_command_line owns inverse tokenization. Distribution unit behavior is observed, not a NVIDIA fact."),
    p(text: "Model independently versioned extdeps.nvidia.linux_driver branches/releases/packages/open-versus-proprietary support; pins remain policy. AMD amdgpu_driver, rocm and amd_smi own kernel/firmware/distribution compatibility and power/clock operations; R9700 catalog figures remain read obligations until cited. GpuDeviceCatalogRow carries each GPU without a power figure; GpuBoardCatalogRow carries each card’s rated power and attachment. A16 is one four-GPU board, not one GPU. Board admission refuses empty GPU population, inverted power range, or default/named point outside it. Catalog owns configurable capability range and zero-power support (A16 does not support it), never the selected operating point."),
    p(text: "extdeps.bmc.supermicro_oem_fan owns mode get/set (Standard/Full/Optimal/HeavyIO/PUE only after reading) and per-zone duty via extdeps.bmc.ipmi; shared raw byte parsing/spelling belongs to ipmitool_raw_reply, including master-write-read/SMpro consumers. BmcFirmwareFamily needs the Supermicro route. H11SSL manual owns slots/lane counts/BIOS labels, headers/pinout and two zones; physical slot order/pitch, CPU-root mapping and header-to-zone mapping are separate read obligations, not facts copied from the handwritten loop."),
    p(text: "Physical residence extends product.placement_supply.PhysicalContainment and gunbc.fleet.fleet_physical_inventory: catalog/serial → host → slot → GPU board position. Census derives host from that authority. H11 identity is opaque under the 2026-10-07 rule, never “h11.” Derive per-slot geometry (order, pitch, clearance to the neighbouring envelope) from the board; adjacency is one input to it, never a refusal by itself. Extend fleet_fan_wiring with direct/splitter/daisy topology and count; tach unreadable behind a chain differs from dead fan. Join board header-zone mapping with installed fans; fan-to-cooled-GPU-position reach is an operator declaration with standing because nothing observes airflow."),
    p(text: "Power-state ladder: Hot retains context/weights/expert cache/KV at normal clocks; ClockParked retains VRAM at minimum clocks (A16 wake ~1–2 s measured, general estimate ~1–3 s); EngineStopped retains host/disk caches with driver persisted (seconds–minutes); HostOff retains durable host state (tens of seconds–minutes). Select cap, park threshold and hysteresis per host/slot/GPU position/fan reach/driver/engine/workload using throughput, card energy, whole-host energy and wake cost. Catalog range is narrowed by device [min,max]; home_serving_power_policy still refuses above TDP. The result is a SelectionReceipt; changed keyed facts mean a different decision."),
    p(text: "Read minimum park clock per device, never hard-code A16’s 405 MHz fleet-wide. Admit park only after lock and equal clocks.mem readback, then reset and above-minimum readback. Refusal/disagreement refuses parking; no cap fallback. A cap constrains load, not idle behavior. Break-even t = E_wake/(P_old−P_new) refuses nonpositive denominator rather than recommending infinity; A16 ClockParked/no-process near-equal GPU power does not justify stopping on GPU energy alone. Wake resets clocks, independently reads reset, then dispatches."),
    p(text: "Fan policy requires an operator amendment: current FirmwareAutomatic resting posture/guard direction does not follow passive A16 temperature. D1(b), recommended and modeled by this graph, is a fixed firmware Full/qualified HeavyIO posture that holds with host dead. D1(a) needs an off-host lease enforcer (BMC or independent fleet process) to force full duty on expiry; a host loop cannot fail safe after its own death. Choosing (a) revises this carrier before realization. Both need accelerator guards and observed firmware behavior with the host controller stopped; that behavior is currently typed unread."),
    p(text: "Converge observes PCI/slot via sysfs + board mapping, loaded driver/version, all tool readings, persistence unit, BMC posture and specimen residue. Plan chooses Noop/Apply/Refuse, consuming selection receipts rather than selecting. Apply pinned packages, required static-unit/persistence ExecStart drop-ins, boot cap oneshot and posture, removing specimens. Independent readback requires LOADED driver = pin, selected cap within both ranges, persistence Enabled after reboot, two-way park/wake P-state movement and BMC posture."),
    p(text: "Driver transition may require DrainRequired/RebootRequired. Never unload/reboot while host holds seats: placement withdraws seats (N14), transition runs, a later independent pass reads loaded driver, then placement readmits. Pending transition is not convergence. Located refusal covers unknown catalog device, unsupported driver, loaded/pinned mismatch, seats blocking drain/reboot, out-of-range cap, nonmodifiable park clock, unmapped header/slot, a passive card with no clearance to its neighbour (adjacency alone is admitted on its measured reading), wrong passive-card zone posture and surviving specimen."),
    h2(text: "6. Measurement instrument"),
    p(text: "N7 creates a gunbc test label, not a disposable script. Every in-bound installed position, including R9700 after arrival, uses this matrix. Every sample MUST carry N13 whole-host wall power and its standing: missing wall power refuses the receipt rather than returning partial evidence. A GPU saving cannot imply host-level sleep savings."),
    CodeBlock { code: "A  idle phases (each 60 s unless stated)
   A1 no client (persistence on)
   A2 bare CUDA/HIP context
   A3 context + 1 GiB allocation
   A4 engine loaded, idle (2-5 min)
   A5 clock-parked (min read from --query-supported-clocks; admitted by lock + readback)
   A6 wake: reset clocks, one warm request -> time to normal clocks + first useful token
   A7 engine stopped, driver persisted (the floor)
B  active power-cap sweep under a representative warm load
   caps from the device min to max in fixed steps; at each: throughput, card energy,
   wall energy, temperature, clock-event reasons -> one throughput-versus-energy curve
C  idle-gap distribution from the router's request trace
   -> the inputs for the park threshold and its hysteresis (minimum dwell, so the card does not thrash)

per sample: host, slot, board position, card + VBIOS, driver + module flavour, persistence,
            engine state, P-state, SM/mem clock, card power + energy counter, temperature,
            zone duty/rpm, whole-host wall power and its standing, CPU package power" },
    h2(text: "7. Dependency graph and validation"),
    p(text: "gpu_card_graph_rows owns nodes, homes, prerequisites and standings. Each change node is one PR; decisions belong to the operator. The witness checks every edge resolves, acyclicity and that every node is an ancestor of G. G is executed host readback, not merged source."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "node"), cell(text: "what"), cell(text: "home"), cell(text: "needs"), cell(text: "standing")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: map(gpu_card_graph_rows, r => gc_row_projection(r: r)),
    },
    p(text: join(["Ready nodes: ", gc_ready_labels(rows: gpu_card_graph_rows), "."], "")),
    p(text: "NVIDIA critical path: N6b residence → N6d reach → N7 instrument → N8 policy → N10 leg → N11 readback; G also waits for D3 and physical R9700 arrival. Choosing D1(a) adds an off-host enforcer before its node starts; a host without BMC PSU-input observation adds a metered-PDU source before measuring. N10 must discriminate on the REAL path: below-min cap, header without zone, a passive card its slot geometry leaves no clearance and reboot under held seats all refuse, while an adjacent pair whose slots and airflow hold it is admitted on its measured reading."),
    p(text: "After this PR merges, generalize the duplicated graph skeleton with gunbc.plans.serving_fleet_program.ServingFleetRow into gunbc.plan, migrating both plans and witnesses together. That sibling-owner change is a named follow-up, not part of this graph’s bound."),
    h2(text: "8. Operator decisions"),
    p(text: "D0 confirms unrecorded hosts of installed A16/Ada pairs through card residence. D1 chooses fixed firmware posture (recommended) or off-host-enforced lease, either amending the fleet ruling. D2 chooses NVIDIA production/new-feature branch and module flavor; recommend one production release whose notes support all Ampere/Ada/Blackwell cards, open modules only if all supported, checking existing 595 server-open first. D3 assigns R9700 host/kernel/distribution. D4 chooses park/wake owner; recommend placement-driven state with host actuator/readback so consolidation sees it; N8 waits for this."),
    h2(text: "9. Boundaries"),
    p(text: "gunbc.plans.serving_fleet_program owns engine deployment, ports/memory slices, pool/router and the live-router edit into #15113; it consumes card states/costs. #15177 owns container toolkit. Fleet consolidation, replica wake choice and host power-off remain routing policy, not this per-card leg."),
  ]
}

data gpu_card_host_program_plan: Plan = Plan {
  slug: "gpu-card-host-program",
  title: "GPU card hosting: drivers, power states, placement and fan zones",
  body: gpu_card_host_program_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen {
    condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Dissolves at G in section 7. No census row is still only committed, and every in-bound card converges through one leg, with its independent readback, the loaded driver included, holding on its host. The leg's refusals have been exercised on the real path: a cap below the device minimum, a header with no zone, a passive card its slot geometry leaves no clearance, and a reboot requested under held seats. None of the section-4 hand-written specimens remains, and every installed position's operating point is a selection receipt rather than a literal. Then this document's content lives in the model's types and the document is deleted."),
  },
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
}
